  abstract = {In this paper, we propose a unified null-space projected Physics-Informed Extreme Learning machine (NP-PIELM) framework that establishes a single non-iterative computational approach for the static bending analysis of plates governed by both Kirchhoff--Love and Reissner--Mindlin plate theory. The proposed formulation enforces: (a) the governing equations in strong form at collocation points and (b) boundary conditions exactly through algebraic null-space projection in coefficient space, guaranteeing strict constraint satisfaction without penalty parameters, Lagrange multipliers or hyperparameter tuning. The framework is intrinsically locking free in case of Reissner--Mindlin formulation. The accuracy and robustness of the NP-PIELM framework is demonstrated through numerical examples. The influence of plate aspect ratio, plate thickness, boundary conditions and geometric skewness is numerically studied. The results confirm that NP-PIELM provides a computationally efficient, geometrically flexible and a unifying framework for analyzing moderately thick to thin plates.}
}

